.SH NAME
kc-vault-unprotect - Allow secrets without Touch ID in a vault


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBkc vault unprotect NAME [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Sets the vault's write policy. A protected vault rejects \fBkc set --no-protect\fR
outright, so production secrets cannot lose Touch ID by accident.
To protect secrets that already exist, use \fBkc protect --all\fR\&.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for unprotect


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--vault\fP=""
	target vault (overrides active vault)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBkc-vault(1)\fP
